# Report 033, phase P5: the CLI page with a keyboard, end to end. The real bundled meshcore-cli (MESHHOP_MESHCLI: phase P4's mccli,
# as installed) runs on Mesh Hop's relay against the simulated board (serial pty; its repeater "Hilltop repeater", admin password
# "password"). Tools > CLI (0.7.0; Home > CLI before), Starting..., the prompt, infos, to the repeater, login with its password masked,
# ver; Help (a command put into the entry, All commands = mccli -h); Esc leaves: meshcore-cli stops, Mesh Hop resumes, Tools is back; a
# message that came during the session is in Chats, no repeater reply is. Run by cli_run.sh (SIMCTL=1) at 640x480 and 800x480.
wait 6000
expect text "Tools"
mark
shot cli01-home
key down
key down
key enter
wait 600
expect text "CLI"
key end
key enter
wait 250
say == Starting (expect cli=waiting or starting, the caption Starting meshcore-cli...)
dump
expect text "Starting meshcore-cli..."
shot cli02-starting
waitstate cli running 40000
waitcli "SimNode> " 5000
say == the prompt (expect cli=running relay=passthrough)
dump
waitstate tab CLI 100
# 0.7.2: opened from Tools, nothing sent yet: the caption says how to pick a repeater (the To... picker is gone)
expect text "Contacts > a repeater > More > Open in CLI, or type: to <name>"
expect notext "Toâ¦"
shot cli03-prompt
check cli-prompt

# a command of the node itself, typed with the keyboard: its answer (infos as JSON)
type infos
key enter
waitcli adv_type 15000
expect clitext "SimNode> infos"
# a message for the deck while the console has the node: meshcore-cli shows it, Mesh Hop reads along (Chats after the session)
sim msg arrives while the CLI runs
waitcli "arrives while the CLI runs" 15000
# the repeater: to, login (the password prompt, the entry in '*', the password never shown), ver (its reply)
type to Hilltop repeater
key enter
waitcli "Hilltop repeater|" 10000
type login
key enter
waitstate cli_pw 1 15000
say == the password prompt (expect cli_pw=1, the entry empty with its password placeholder)
dump
shot cli04-password-prompt
type password
waitstate cli_entry ******** 2000
shot cli05-password-typed
key enter
waitcli "Login success" 15000
expect noclitext ": password"
expect noclitext "> password"
waitstate cli_pw 0 1000
type ver
key enter
waitcli "v1.15.0-sim" 15000
say == the repeater's answers in the output (expect cli_masked=8)
dump
shot cli06-output
check cli-output
# Up: the history (this run only; the password is not in it)
key up
waitstate cli_entry ver 1000
key up
waitstate cli_entry login 1000
key down
key down
waitstate cli_entry "" 1000
# PgUp scrolls back (the view stops following), PgDn goes back to the bottom
key pgup
waitstate cli_follow 0 1000
key pgdn
waitstate cli_follow 1 1000

# Help (Ctrl+H): the curated list; Enter on a command puts it into the entry and goes back to the console
key ctrl-h
waitstate cli_help 1 2000
expect text "HOW IT WORKS"
shot cli07-help
check cli-help
key down
key down
key enter
waitstate cli_help 0 2000
waitstate cli_entry / 1000
key bksp
# All commands: meshcore-cli -h of the bundle
key ctrl-h
waitstate cli_help 1 2000
key end
key enter
waitstate cli_help 2 2000
waitstate cli_usage 2 30000
shot cli08-all-commands
key esc
waitstate cli_help 1 1000
key esc
waitstate cli_help 0 1000

# Ctrl+C sends the interrupt: at its prompt meshcore-cli (prompt_toolkit) takes it as the end of the session
key ctrl-c
waitstate cli ended 8000
say == after Ctrl+C (expect cli=ended cli_end='meshcore-cli ended' relay=off)
dump
shot cli08b-interrupted

# Esc leaves: meshcore-cli stops, the relay closes, Mesh Hop resumes and reads the node again; Tools is back (0.7.0: the CLI is one of
# its rows)
key esc
waitstate tab Tools 2000
waitstate cli off 2000
waitstate relay off 8000
say == back on Tools after the CLI (expect cli=off relay=off home=0 tab=Tools)
dump
shot cli09-home-after
# Chats (Tab twice: Settings, Chats): the message of the session is there; no reply of the repeater became a chat
expect more all_msgs
key tab
key tab
wait 800
expect notext "Hilltop repeater"
shot cli10-chats-after
